# L §3.2 (round 12): "A row's value has its type's unit at every key it states, so a row that leaves such a key
# unstated or * gives one unit for keys of several and is refused (LOAD-UNIT), unless its value is a bare literal, which
# takes each key's unit (Inline figures, above)". amt is num c per currency c: `amt[*] = 5 PLN` is refused; `amt2[*] =
# 5`, a bare literal, is 5 PLN at PLN and 5 EUR at EUR. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §3.2, writer 5's T-10.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
input amt[c in currencies]: num c

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt[*] = 5 PLN

ask q: amt[PLN]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT 5 gives one unit for keys of several units ...
